      "content_markdown": "Example 24. Let Universal set be $U = \\{x : x \\in N \\text{ and } x \\le 6\\}$, $A = \\{x : x \\text{ prime and } x \\le 5\\}$, $B = \\{x : x \\text{ even number and } x \\le 6\\}$ and $C = A \\setminus B$\n1) Determine $A^c$.\n2) Prove that, $A \\cup B = (A \\setminus B) \\cup (B \\setminus A) \\cup (A \\cap B)$\n3) Prove that, $(A \\cap C) \\times B = (A \\times B) \\cap (C \\times B)$",
      "activity_tag": null
